| `... - Refund requested` | `7431:57219` | Session stays `Canceled`. **Mark for refund** is Primary Brand, sits right. Reassign stays Tertiary — ops can still flip to a substitute. |
| `... - Refunded` | `7431:84864` | Mark for refund gone, a `Refund` row records *marked refunded · when · by admin*, and the quiet **Refunded** label joins the session in the rail (same treatment as Session 03). |

Panel (760, confirm shell): heading → **Sessions to reassign** (checkbox rows, canceled one pre-checked, others selectable) → read-only note from the sitter → **New sitter · Approved only** (search + rows, selected row = `#fff6f6` fill / `#ef5c59` stroke, View profile) → Cancel (Terciary) · **Assign sitter** (Primary **Brand**, not Error — reassign is not destructive).

**One sitter per pass.** To send two sessions to two different sitters, ops runs the panel twice. No per-session sitter picker. Sessions still without a substitute get **no flag and no counter** — they stay `Canceled`.

**The owner is never told in the app.** Customer service handles it over WhatsApp. Admin is the only record, so the swap must stay visible on our side (activity log line, from → to).

## Tables

**`.row` is a column, not a row.** Each `.row` holds one `.tableheader item`
followed by N `.tablecell item` instances stacked vertically. Tables are
assembled column-major, left to right. On the reference page the columns sit at
x = 0, 50, 222, 411, 558, 685, 797, 887, 1006 (first is the 50px checkbox column).

**Row height is 50, cell insets are 10 left / 11 top.** This breaks the 4px rule
and that is intentional — new tables match the existing 50px rhythm so they line
up with current screens. A 4px migration is a separate future cleanup.

Column widths may total slightly more than 1128 (reference sums to 1131), which
drives the horizontal scrollbar. That is deliberate, not a mistake.

