## Modals and overlays

Screen frames are **HORIZONTAL auto layout** (sidebar + content column). Anything
overlaid on top — dim rectangle, modal, popup — must be set to
`layoutPositioning = 'ABSOLUTE'` before its x/y will hold. Otherwise auto layout
pushes it out to the right of the content column.

Dim overlay: black at 70% opacity, 1440×1024, absolute at (0,0). Taller screens (this list is 1171) stretch the dim to the frame height.

**Notifications overlay** (`Pet Owner List - Table View - Notifications`, `7907:113085`) sits to the right of Pet Owner List (`7893:108707`). Same list, plus dim + right `Notification panel` (`7900:109587`, 440×frame height, absolute x=1000). Bell on `Notifications/profile` opens this frame. Close goes Back. Rows are `Notification item` Unread/Read (`7899:109509`): brand-light fill + coral dot when unread. Header: title · unread count · Mark all as read (Small Secondary Brand) · `dark/Icon/x`. Footer: **Delete all**. Dummy: new owner, document uploaded, booking completed, pending verification. **Delete all** opens the same 659 `Pop up` as other destructive confirms: “Are you sure you want to delete all notifications?” · Cancel Tertiary · Delete Primary Error. Extra dim 70% over the open panel. Reuse the panel instance on any 1440 screen — do not restyle.

**Profile overlay** (`Pet Owner List - Table View - Profile`, `7918:111704`) sits to the right of the notifications overlay. Same dim + right `Profile panel` (`7918:111667`, 440×frame height, absolute x=1000). Avatar / name on `Notifications/profile` opens this frame. Close goes Back. Header: Profile · `dark/Icon/x`. Identity: chrome photo · **Vukasin Minic** · Role **Admin** · email `vukasinminic03@gmail.com`. Actions are `Profile action` rows (`7918:111655`): **Reset password** (lock) · **Log out** (`dark/Icon/log-in` — the set has no log-out glyph). No reset form on this overlay — menu only. Reuse the panel instance on any 1440 screen — do not restyle. **Reset password** opens **Profile - Recovery sent** (`7923:112473`): same drawer, bottom 392 card, success check from Recovery email sent, copy **Recovery email sent** / *We sent you a recovery email on vukasinminic03@gmail.com. The link provided wil be valid for 2 hour.* Card X goes Back.

Modal container: VERTICAL auto layout, hug height, fixed width (760 on the
passport modal), padding 32 top / 24 sides / 24 bottom, gap 24, corner radius 24.

Content order inside a modal, top to bottom: heading, then **editable fields**,
then read-only info rows, then media, then the action row. Editable controls come
before the data they modify — do not bury the status field under the read-only
block.

Inputs are **not** full width. Size them to what the content needs (the status
select is 344 in a 760 modal), even though the rows around them fill.

`.info row item` rows: label column fixed at 122, value FILL, 20 gap between rows.
Abbreviate labels to match the table conventions elsewhere — `MC number`,
`MC expiry date`, not the full words.

Action row: FILL width with `primaryAxisAlignItems = 'MAX'` to right-align, gap 12.
Cancel is `Hierarchy=Terciary`, the confirming button is `Hierarchy=Primary`.

## Buttons — brand vs error

`Button` has a `Brand/Error` variant property. **`Error` means destructive.** Use
it only for actions that delete or otherwise cannot be undone. Everything else,
including Save changes, uses `Brand` — that is `#ef5c59`, the same coral as
"+ Add new".

## Input Filed — icons

`Input Filed` (note the typo in the component name) carries its own icon slots.
To make a select, set the boolean `Right Icon#18194:296` to true and swap
`↪ Right Icon#18194:309` to `dark/Icon/chevron-down`. Never place a separate
chevron instance next to the field.

